content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23110, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.2 mm/s against Figure 3 severity zones: Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'). This is above the Zone A/B boundary of 2.8 mm/s and below the Zone C boundary of 4.5 mm/s. It is well short of the Zone D stop limit of 7.1 mm/s, so the site 'highest severity zone' stop rule is not triggered. The report does not say whether the reading is RMS or which housing it was taken on, and the manual requires classifying the highest reading of both housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature 68 C against the manual limits (normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C): within the normal band, 2 C below the normal limit and 12 C below alarm. The site P1 rule (temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit) is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal drip of about one drop every two seconds: the evidence gives no numeric acceptance limit for seal leakage. The troubleshooting table treats any leakage at the shaft seal as a fault, with corrective action to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall: no reading reaches a stop or alarm threshold, so the pump does not need to be stopped immediately. The seal leak requires planned seal replacement, so the work order is P2 (planned).",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces. If the originally fitted component seal HF3-450 is installed, early failure is a known issue on pumps from serial HF3-22000, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance. Serial HF3-23110 is in this range.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal has run dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge and the seal must never run dry; check the flush line for blockage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. Vibration is in Zone B rather than Zone A, which is consistent with, though not proof of, misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before isolation, record vibration on both bearing housings (mm/s RMS) and the non-drive-end housing temperature. Classify the highest vibration reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply site isolation: electrical LOTO at the MCC and close and lock the suction and discharge valves. Obtain a line-break permit, then drain and vent the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and rig certified lifting equipment. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect the shaft sleeve for scoring and replace sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Record which seal type was fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, NOT HF3-450. It is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the seal gland nuts (M10) to 30 Nm per SB-2026-014, not the 25 Nm in Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm, lightly oiled threads (Table 5).",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reinstall the back pull-out assembly. Tighten the casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm and, if disturbed, the bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm, lightly oiled threads (Table 5).",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm, angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Correct if outside tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is clear. Fill and vent the casing before start so the seal never runs dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, remeasure vibration on both bearing housings and the bearing housing temperatures. Confirm vibration is no higher than Zone B, temperature is below 70 C, and the seal is not leaking.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Have one on hand; fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC before any work inside the pump or on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit; drain and vent the pump first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly (68 kg) exceeds the 25 kg site limit. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry on restart. Ensure the casing is full and the Plan 11 flush is working.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration on either housing reaches Zone D (7.1 mm/s RMS or above), stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 hours, 2 technicians (standard time is for the component seal; the cartridge seal may differ).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Planned total: about 5.5 hours elapsed, about 9.5 technician-hours (2 x 4.0 h plus 1 x 1.5 h). This excludes isolation, permit and lifting-plan preparation time.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list (Rev D) gives component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says do NOT fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 and use HF3-450B. P-108 is serial HF3-23110, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B is to be fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because the bulletin applies to serial HF3-23110 and HF3-450B is being fitted, use 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve inspection: the manual says only to inspect the sleeve for scoring. The bulletin, which applies to this serial, adds a replacement criterion of more than 0.1 mm scoring depth and states that no sleeve measurement is needed with the pre-set cartridge seal. Apply the bulletin criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other Table 5 torques (casing bolts 210 Nm, impeller nut 160 Nm, bearing housing bolts 85 Nm) are not addressed by the bulletin. They are used here as the only documented values, although the bulletin's wording ('pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use ... Table 5') leaves their status for this serial unconfirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "No documented acceptance limit for seal leakage rate; the severity of one drop every two seconds cannot be quantified from the evidence.",
    "Which seal is currently fitted to P-108 (HF3-450 or HF3-450B)? This determines whether the known early-failure issue is the likely cause.",
    "Is the 3.2 mm/s reading RMS, and on which bearing housing was it taken? The non-drive-end vibration and temperature were not reported.",
    "Is the raw-water transfer line chemically dosed? If so, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required.",
    "Confirm with AquaDyne that the remaining Table 5 torques (casing, impeller nut, bearing housing bolts) still apply to pumps at serial HF3-22000 and above.",
    "Standard labour time for fitting the cartridge seal HF3-450B is not given; Table 6 may reflect the component seal.",
    "Is there a recorded alignment baseline or history for P-108 to judge whether misalignment has developed?"
  ]
}
